The app had no URL state — selecting Shabbat 65 kept the URL at `/`, making deep links and sharing impossible. This adds `history.pushState`-based routing so the URL reflects the current selection and direct navigation to e.g. `/Shabbat/65` restores the full UI state.

## URL updates on selection
- **Seder** → `pushState('/')`
- **Maseches** → `pushState('/Shabbat')` (spaces → underscores for multi-word tractates)
- **Daf** → `pushState('/Shabbat/65')`

`selectSeder`, `selectMaseches`, `selectDaf` each gain an `updateUrl = true` parameter; internal restoration calls pass `false` to skip pushing duplicate history entries.

## State restoration from URL
`restoreFromPath(path)` parses the pathname and drives the three-step selection UI programmatically. Called on:
- **`DOMContentLoaded`** — restores state on initial load or after `404.html` redirect
- **`popstate`** — resets and restores on browser back/forward

## Static-host deep link support (`404.html`)
On static hosts (GitHub Pages), `/Shabbat/65` returns a 404. A new `404.html` saves the original path to `sessionStorage` and bounces to `/`; `index.html` then reads, validates, and applies it via `history.replaceState` before restoring.

```js
// 404.html
sessionStorage.setItem('redirect', window.location.pathname);
window.location.replace('/');

// index.html – DOMContentLoaded
const redirectPath = sessionStorage.getItem('redirect');
if (redirectPath) {
  sessionStorage.removeItem('redirect');
  if (/^\/[A-Za-z_]+(\/\d+)?$/.test(redirectPath)) {   // validate before use
    history.replaceState(null, '', redirectPath);
  }
}
restoreFromPath(window.location.pathname);
```

The regex validation on the `sessionStorage` value prevents arbitrary path injection.

Bootstraps a client-side photo upload interface for the otherwise-empty Nasim repository.

## What's included

- **`index.html`** – Upload page with a drag-and-drop zone, file `<input>`, image preview, file metadata display, and Remove/Upload action buttons. ARIA roles and keyboard navigation (Enter/Space on drop zone) included.
- **`style.css`** – Responsive layout via CSS custom properties; drag-over highlight, progress bar, and button states.
- **`script.js`** – Validates type (`image/jpeg|png|gif|webp`) and size (≤ 10 MB), renders a `FileReader` preview, and animates an upload progress bar on submit.

## Key behaviour

```js
// File guard before any processing
if (!ALLOWED_TYPES.includes(file.type)) { showStatus('Unsupported file type…', 'error'); return; }
if (file.size > MAX_FILE_SIZE)          { showStatus('File is too large…',       'error'); return; }

// Preview via FileReader
var reader = new FileReader();
reader.onload = function (e) { previewImage.src = e.target.result; … };
reader.readAsDataURL(file);
```

No build tooling or dependencies — plain HTML/CSS/JS.

